  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. The bog witch starts hostile, the only NPC in the short suite to do so, and she is not a combatant. Inputs 14 and 17 move her up to unfriendly and then neutral; input 21 moves her back down to unfriendly. Her replies at input 16 should be cold, and narration of her as warm or friendly anywhere is a RELATION divergence. Input 2 has disadvantage from the scenario because of the fog. Fire Bolt is a cantrip; Cure Wounds at inputs 13 and 25 spends both of Corin's slots. Input 12 is a narration-only turn that invites a hit-point band phrase about Corin. Input 22 asks for a potion that is not in state, to test PHANTOM detection; its expected call is null. The village and its people are not in state, so narration that names a villager is a phantom character. Inputs 4 to 11 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game."
